// there must be one and only one line that starts with a "*"
// that entry will be become a part of the standard subject line
// FieldId as it appears in outgoing message (followed by a ": ")
// FieldName, does not appear anywhere, currently if it contains "Date" or "Time" triggers a validity check (or it will soon)
// Type, can be "str" for string, "mstr" for multiline string, "rb" for a set of radio buttons, "cb" for a checkbox
// RequireFlag, must be Y or N or blank (same as N)
// ValidityCheck, if blank it just means "any entry", otherewise is a function name
// 4 numbers for the location on screen, assumes 850x1100 image (100dpi), upper left and lower right, both inclusive, for radio buttons is a box that encloses all of them
// if the ending x or ending y starts with a "+", it is relative to the starting x or y
// if the ending x or ending y is a 0, the code uses a default width or height

// Next fields are only for radio buttons, they are in groups of 5, one for each radio button
// First is the string that will be sent as the value for this button choice
// Then 4 numbers for the location on screen, same details as for the main location

